<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31753" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-nūbĭlo</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to cover with
				clouds</i> or <i>fog; to overcloud, darken,
				obscure</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultūs serenitatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haec omnia vitium,</span>”
				<i>to obscure</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 4, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">odore sulfuris obnubilatus,</span>”
				<i>beclouded, stupefied, senseless</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 228, 22</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8</span></i>
			, p. 204, 38.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
